From b9523a711ac82c781e964c068d707cd5a38dfa5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hyunW3 <0176778602@naver.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Jun 2026 16:34:53 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 21/22] aunet/eval: route BPEByte generate_until through bt
 online generation

Port of spacebyte_feasibility commit d4669a1 (_model_generate override): make
generation-based downstream evals (gsm8k, nq_open, triviaqa, mgsm, bbh, ...)
use the backtracking online loop for BPEByte models, so generated text is
conditioned on the correct before-root patch boundaries instead of the
degenerate "every byte a boundary" structure get_levels_mask_gen produces.

- generate_bt.py: online_bt_loop / generate_online_bt gain stops + eos for
  early exit (a row halts when its generated tail ends with a stop sequence or
  eos), so generation isn't forced to max_gen_len each example.
- eval.py: EvalHarnessLM.generate_until detects a bpe_* patch strategy and
  routes to the new _generate_until_bt, which reuses the same gen-arg grouping
  and byte-length scaling, honors stops in-loop, and truncates the answer at the
  first stop. Word-strategy (AU-Net 2) keeps the stock cached path.
- test_generate_bt.py: add stop-sequence + eos early-exit test (6 total).

Note: this eval.py commit also carries the pre-existing (uncommitted) generate_
until rework it builds on (gen-arg grouping, GEN_BYTES_PER_TOKEN scaling,
max_until_size fix); the two are inseparable in one function.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
